WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.041 --> 00:00:35.041
In Chapter 4,

2
00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:36.750
Lord Krishna explained

3
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.833
to Arjuna the importance of knowledge.

4
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:43.166
He described how a wise person,

5
00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:45.625
unattached to the fruits of their actions,

6
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:47.666
performs their duties

7
00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:50.750
and progresses towards spiritual liberation.

8
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.791
However, most people believe

9
00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:58.916
that once they attain knowledge,
 there is no need for action.

10
00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:01.500
Many intellectuals even think that

11
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.666
once you gain knowledge,

12
00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:06.500
what more can actions provide?

13
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.208
But this is a misconception,

14
00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:11.666
not the true wisdom of the Gita.

15
00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:14.041
This very misconception

16
00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:16.375
is causing Arjuna's dilemma.

17
00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.833
Along with glorifying knowledge,

18
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:22.750
Lord Krishna also instructed Arjuna to fight,

19
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.750
which Arjuna sees as a contradiction.

20
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.250
Arjuna expresses this dilemma

21
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.458
in the present verse.

22
00:01:30.458 --> 00:01:31.916
He asks

23
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:34.166
whether one should renounce action

24
00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:36.791
or engage in it.

25
00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:39.166
Recall that Arjuna posed

26
00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:42.833
a similar question at the start of Chapter 3.

27
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:46.125
Now, with this verse, begins

28
00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:48.208
Chapter 5,

29
00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.750
where Lord Krishna will illuminate

30
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.625
the profound truth of

31
00:01:52.625 --> 00:01:55.375
selfless action, (Nishkam Karma Yoga.)

32
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.583
In Chapter

33
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:02.541
4,

34
00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:05.958
Lord Krishna taught the 
path of Nishkam Karma Yoga

35
00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.083
and explained how,

36
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:10.916
by following that very path,

37
00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:14.333
one attains knowledge.

38
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:17.875
Yet, at the end of the 4th chapter,

39
00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:19.500
Lord Krishna also encourages

40
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.541
Arjuna to fight.

41
00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.541
Now Arjuna wonders,

42
00:02:23.541 --> 00:02:25.333
once knowledge is attained,

43
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:27.958
what is the relevance of action?

44
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:30.625
That's why he's asking here

45
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:33.250
which is better –

46
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.250
to renounce action

47
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.041
or to engage in it?

48
00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:40.750
This is Arjuna's dilemma.

49
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:44.333
Have you ever found yourself 
in a similar predicament,

50
00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:49.250
unsure whether to pursue a 
course of action? or not?

51
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.500
To resolve this,

52
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.416
you need to understand one thing –

53
00:02:54.416 --> 00:02:58.291
That knowledge and action are not opposites,

54
00:02:58.291 --> 00:03:01.666
but rather complement each other.

55
00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:04.250
In the Gita, Lord Krishna

56
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.750
is making Arjuna understand, through His teachings,

57
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.291
that one should perform actions

58
00:03:08.291 --> 00:03:10.250
as a matter of duty.

59
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.791
But how can this be done?

60
00:03:13.791 --> 00:03:14.625
How can we

61
00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:15.583
fulfill our actions,

62
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:17.416
seeing them

63
00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:19.458
as our duty?

64
00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:21.625
It's only possible

65
00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:25.500
when we act without 
considering ourselves the sole doer.

66
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.375
And when you do so,

67
00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.250
you will no longer be attached

68
00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.333
to the results of those actions.

69
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.583
When you perform your duty without

70
00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:37.791
attachment to its fruits,

71
00:03:37.791 --> 00:03:39.916
such enlightened action

72
00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:42.291
is called Nishkam Karma.

73
00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:44.666
Though both paths of knowledge and action

74
00:03:44.666 --> 00:03:46.791
lead to liberation...

75
00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:49.291
But, for most people,

76
00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:51.291
the path of selfless action is simpler

77
00:03:51.291 --> 00:03:52.750
while fulfilling one's worldly responsibilities

78
00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.375
and more practical.

79
00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:57.500
In Chapter 5, Lord Krishna 
will make Arjuna understand

80
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.083
that renunciation doesn't mean

81
00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:03.041
abandoning action altogether.

82
00:04:03.041 --> 00:04:05.541
True renunciation means giving up the anxiety

83
00:04:05.541 --> 00:04:09.041
over your action's outcomes.

84
00:04:09.041 --> 00:04:11.916
If you must renounce something,

85
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:14.916
renounce not your actions,

86
00:04:14.916 --> 00:04:18.416
but your attachment to their fruits.

87
00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:30.500
Imagine you're at a juncture in life

88
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.750
where two paths diverge.

89
00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.791
On one path,

90
00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:37.916
it seems that if you

91
00:04:37.916 --> 00:04:40.291
renounce everything and

92
00:04:40.291 --> 00:04:44.166
turn away from action,

93
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:46.625
you'll find peace.

94
00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:50.458
But on the other,

95
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:58.250
you'll face the toughest 
challenges and adversities.

96
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:03.000
Arjuna is at such a crossroads.

97
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
One path tells him to

98
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.916
abandon everything, renounce the war,

99
00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:14.458
and pursue knowledge and peace.

100
00:05:14.458 --> 00:05:16.166
But

101
00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:18.333
the other path

102
00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:20.291
the other path

103
00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:25.083
inspires him to do his duty.

104
00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:29.458
Don’t you too sometimes feel

105
00:05:29.458 --> 00:05:32.541
that far from the ever-increasing demands

106
00:05:32.541 --> 00:05:37.375
of this busy modern world,

107
00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:43.666
Is it only in solitude that 
peace and knowledge are found?

108
00:05:43.666 --> 00:05:46.541
It may feel natural to have a thought like that,

109
00:05:46.541 --> 00:05:49.583
but

110
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:50.541
this path

111
00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:53.750
will bring you neither peace

112
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.291
nor true knowledge.

113
00:05:57.291 --> 00:06:01.500
Let's understand this with an example.

114
00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.708
A potter

115
00:06:03.708 --> 00:06:07.916
shapes the clay on a spinning wheel.

116
00:06:07.916 --> 00:06:12.250
The work isn't easy, but he does it.

117
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.500
The potter knows the pot being made

118
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:21.083
will not come about solely through his efforts.

119
00:06:21.083 --> 00:06:23.541
In this process of pottery,

120
00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:25.458
the nature of the clay,

121
00:06:25.458 --> 00:06:28.250
the spinning wheel, and his hands –

122
00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:34.125
all three contribute to the pot's creation.

123
00:06:34.125 --> 00:06:35.625
Thus,

124
00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:38.125
while performing his actions,

125
00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:42.833
without considering himself the sole doer,

126
00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:49.500
he remains unattached to the 
fruits of his labor and experiences peace.

127
00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.750
Similarly,

128
00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.541
when we perform our actions
 as a matter of duty,

129
00:06:54.541 --> 00:07:00.250
unattached to the results,

130
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.916
that is when, we attain both peace

131
00:07:03.916 --> 00:07:06.541
and knowledge.

132
00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:08.041
So, the next time

133
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:12.208
you feel like shying away
 from your responsibilities,

134
00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:15.583
do consider this:

135
00:07:15.583 --> 00:07:18.833
true happiness and peace

136
00:07:18.833 --> 00:07:22.833
are found in performing your duty

137
00:07:22.833 --> 00:07:28.125
without attachment to the outcome.

138
00:07:32.916 --> 00:07:37.791
Arjuna faces a moral dilemma

139
00:07:37.791 --> 00:07:43.500
should he raise weapons 
against his own kinsmen in war

140
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.541
or turn away from the battle?

141
00:07:47.541 --> 00:07:51.208
Just like Arjuna, you too 
must encounter such dilemmas

142
00:07:51.208 --> 00:07:53.125
in your social

143
00:07:53.125 --> 00:07:56.916
or family life.

144
00:07:56.916 --> 00:07:59.166
In a family, there are as many perspectives
 as there are members,

145
00:07:59.166 --> 00:08:03.625
or in your group, as many
 outlooks as there are friends;

146
00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:06.541
There are that many perspectives.

147
00:08:06.541 --> 00:08:11.333
Everyone has their own expectations.

148
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:13.291
Amidst this,

149
00:08:13.291 --> 00:08:16.708
while juggling your personal, professional,

150
00:08:16.708 --> 00:08:21.375
and family life,

151
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:23.500
do you sometimes feel overwhelmed

152
00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:28.125
by the burden of your responsibilities?

153
00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:30.750
And such pressure breeds dilemmas.

154
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.625
Think of it like this...

155
00:08:33.625 --> 00:08:36.000
Does a mother ever

156
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.541
consider cooking

157
00:08:37.541 --> 00:08:40.833
for her family a burden?

158
00:08:40.833 --> 00:08:43.166
Or does a father ever tire

159
00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:47.208
of earning for his family?

160
00:08:47.208 --> 00:08:50.291
Praise or criticism –

161
00:08:50.291 --> 00:08:53.250
this process goes on day after day,

162
00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.583
year after year.

163
00:08:56.583 --> 00:08:58.666
Similarly,

164
00:08:58.666 --> 00:09:02.583
don't see your responsibilities as burdens.

165
00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:07.958
Change your attitude towards your them.

166
00:09:07.958 --> 00:09:12.208
What if every family 
member wholeheartedly fulfills

167
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:17.083
their every duty?

168
00:09:17.083 --> 00:09:18.166
It will create

169
00:09:18.166 --> 00:09:21.833
an environment of such enthusiasm

170
00:09:21.833 --> 00:09:26.458
where you won't shy away from any obligation;

171
00:09:26.458 --> 00:09:28.833
you'll be motivated to embrace

172
00:09:28.833 --> 00:09:32.708
each new challenge with an open mind.

173
00:09:32.708 --> 00:09:36.666
This duty, performed with a spirit of service,

174
00:09:36.666 --> 00:09:41.166
will bind the family in an unbreakable bond.

175
00:09:41.166 --> 00:09:43.166
Now you tell me,

176
00:09:43.166 --> 00:09:49.875
Would you like to create such a family?

177
00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.291
In business, you often get entangled in situations

178
00:09:57.291 --> 00:10:05.333
where you either confront
 the problem with full force

179
00:10:05.333 --> 00:10:10.250
or sit idle, hands over hands.

180
00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.750
Just like Arjuna,

181
00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.666
do you too get caught

182
00:10:15.666 --> 00:10:20.375
in such moral dilemmas in your professional life?

183
00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:23.333
Why view the problem or solution

184
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.083
like black and white

185
00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:27.583
or water and fire, as two

186
00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:31.208
opposing extremes?

187
00:10:31.208 --> 00:10:33.750
Let's understand this with an example.

188
00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.250
Consider

189
00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.708
a project manager

190
00:10:38.708 --> 00:10:41.375
in an organization.

191
00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:43.750
He has two options:

192
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.833
One – insist that project members

193
00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:51.625
strictly adhere to deadlines at every stage

194
00:10:51.625 --> 00:10:55.916
to ensure timely, high-quality work.

195
00:10:55.916 --> 00:10:58.583
The second option –

196
00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:00.875
give the project

197
00:11:00.875 --> 00:11:02.500
members

198
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.500
complete freedom

199
00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:09.083
to come up with new ideas.

200
00:11:09.083 --> 00:11:14.708
But while new ideas will enhance the work,

201
00:11:14.708 --> 00:11:19.833
there’s a possibility that 
it may not get done on time.

202
00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:24.375
Deadline adherence or new ideas –

203
00:11:24.375 --> 00:11:26.958
these are two options.

204
00:11:26.958 --> 00:11:28.416
But

205
00:11:28.416 --> 00:11:30.958
you've confined the problem to options

206
00:11:30.958 --> 00:11:34.708
at two opposing ends.

207
00:11:34.708 --> 00:11:40.750
Either this or that... Now a third option –

208
00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.416
an approach where

209
00:11:43.416 --> 00:11:48.083
the manager talks to his members,

210
00:11:48.083 --> 00:11:51.333
sets deadlines by consensus

211
00:11:51.333 --> 00:11:56.291
while giving them freedom.

212
00:11:56.291 --> 00:11:57.291
Won't this

213
00:11:57.291 --> 00:12:01.041
fulfill all objectives?

214
00:12:01.041 --> 00:12:04.916
In the third option, members are free,

215
00:12:04.916 --> 00:12:06.791
and deadlines will be met

216
00:12:06.791 --> 00:12:10.125
along with new ideas.

217
00:12:10.125 --> 00:12:13.041
It's likely this will lead to

218
00:12:13.041 --> 00:12:16.708
good work in the organization.

219
00:12:16.708 --> 00:12:19.166
Be steadfast like a mountain

220
00:12:19.166 --> 00:12:22.208
in your resolve and flexible

221
00:12:22.208 --> 00:12:25.833
like grass in your approach.

222
00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:27.208
Positive thinking

223
00:12:27.208 --> 00:12:31.041
is only possible with freedom

224
00:12:31.041 --> 00:12:36.708
because bondage only breeds helplessness.

225
00:12:36.708 --> 00:12:39.708
Do give this a thought.
